meta {
  name: WebSocket Connect (wscat example)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # WebSocket Live Stream

  Bruno CLI does not support WebSocket connections. Use wscat for interactive
  testing or the Streamlit dashboard for a visual stream.

  ## Connect with wscat

  ```bash
  # Install wscat once
  npm install -g wscat

  # Connect without auth (open endpoint during MVP)
  wscat -c "ws://localhost:8000/ws/observations/stream"

  # Connect with bearer token (when auth is enabled)
  wscat -c "ws://localhost:8000/ws/observations/stream?token=<your-token>"
  ```

  ## Expected events

  Each drift event is pushed as a JSON object:

  ```json
  {
    "event": "drift",
    "source_id": 1,
    "severity": "minor",
    "detected_at": "2026-05-25T10:00:00Z"
  }
  ```

  ## Streamlit dashboard

  Run the dashboard for a browser-based live tail:

  ```bash
  uv run streamlit run services/dashboard/streamlit_app.py
  ```

  This GET /health request is included as a smoke check so `bru run` does not
  skip this collection folder.
}
